{"id": "DemnYE2vTUg", "title": "Video by nick_saraev", "description": "Comment \"DESIGN\" to get this skill to create smooth animations with Claude Code.\n\nClaude Code can now create these clean line animations that react to your cursor.\n\nThe lines move as your cursor moves.\n\nAnd it all comes from a simple prompt.\n\nIt's a free skill called Hairline.\n\nIt teaches your Claude the exact 10 design rules behind this style.\n\nThe 10 rules are what keep everything looking clean.\n\nThink of it like handing Claude a style guide.\n\nYou just describe your idea to Claude.\n\nSomething like a hero or pricing section for your website.\n\nEven a short description is enough to start.\n\nAnd it gives you a bunch of concepts.\n\nEach concept gives you a different direction.\n\nSo you're not stuck with just one idea.\n\nThen you just pick the one you like.\n\nAnd it builds an animated component.\n\nYou can drop it straight into your websites, decks, mobile apps, or wherever you want.\n\nYou don't have to design every detail by hand.\n\nThat's three steps from idea to finished animation.\n\nDescribe it, pick one, and drop it in.\n\nSo the whole page feels alive.\n\nThink of it like a design studio inside Claude Code.\n\nHairline is free, so there's nothing to lose.\n\nIt's a small skill with a big visual payoff.\n\n#claudecode #hairlineskill #claudedesign #aianimations #animatedcomponents", "channel": "nick_saraev", "uploader_id": "72269881052", "uploader": "Nick Saraev", "timestamp": 1792257175, "like_count": 805, "comment_count": 546, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1590999296039096a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 67.567, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.famd5-4.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQPmOPm43LGifneYLyzk5VSgWLPHgIydrkdnFvUcYpHHUVvq-uLMpAiRx3cUFRQybOXZ7tbCipqB8-93VsTTy_7gJfRl1a150HlxQyg.mp4?_nc_cat=101&_nc_oc=Adpql6e